OVERVIEW: Start the DICOM server

Start a DICOM server that accepts incoming connections and
handles C-ECHO, C-FIND, C-STORE, C-MOVE, and C-GET requests.

USAGE: dicom-server start <options>

OPTIONS:
  -a, --aet <aet>         Application Entity Title (default: DICOMKIT_SCP)
  -p, --port <port>       Port to listen on (default: 11112)
  --data-dir <data-dir>   Data directory for storing DICOM files (default:
                          ./dicom-data)
  --database <database>   Index mode: filesystem (durable startup reindex,
                          default) or none (unindexed); SQLite/PostgreSQL
                          unavailable (default: filesystem)
  --database-url <database-url>
                          Index connection string: filesystem://;
                          SQLite/PostgreSQL URLs are refused. Use --database
                          none to disable indexing
  --config <config>       Configuration file path
  --max-connections <max-connections>
                          Maximum concurrent connections (default: 10)
  --max-pdu-size <max-pdu-size>
                          Maximum PDU size in bytes (default: 16384)
  --allowed-ae <allowed-ae>
                          Allowed calling AE titles (comma-separated)
  --blocked-ae <blocked-ae>
                          Blocked calling AE titles (comma-separated)
  --move-destination <move-destination>
                          C-MOVE destination as AE=host:port (repeatable); an
                          unknown Move Destination is refused with A801
  -v, --verbose           Verbose logging
  --tls                   Request TLS (not implemented; refused without
                          starting an unsecured listener)
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

